{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1712","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Woeful Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I wonder, does the falling rain"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Forever yearn for it's disdain?"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Effluvium of the Mind"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a positive integer $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find any permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$ such that the sum $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(1,p_1) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, p_2) + \\ldots + \\operatorname{lcm}(n, p_n)$$$ is as large as possible. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Least_common_multiple"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"least common multiple (LCM)"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A permutation is an array consisting of $$$n$$$ distinct integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in arbitrary order. For example, $$$[2,3,1,5,4]$$$ is a permutation, but $$$[1,2,2]$$$ is not a permutation ($$$2$$$ appears twice in the array) and $$$[1,3,4]$$$ is also not a permutation ($$$n=3$$$ but there is $$$4$$$ in the array)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1\\,000$$$). Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line for each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case print $$$n$$$ integers $$$p_1$$$, $$$p_2$$$, $$$\\ldots$$$, $$$p_n$$$ — the permutation with the maximum possible value of $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(1,p_1) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, p_2) + \\ldots + \\operatorname{lcm}(n, p_n)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 \n2 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n = 1$$$, there is only one permutation, so the answer is $$$[1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n = 2$$$, there are two permutations: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1, 2]$$$ — the sum is $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(1,1) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, 2) = 1 + 2 = 3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2, 1]$$$ — the sum is $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(1,2) + \\operatorname{lcm}(2, 1) = 2 + 2 = 4$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1712B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1712/problem/B"}